{"abstract":[{"text":"The Map is the first screen in LinkMap. It stays visible even before you choose a Project.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Map"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Map"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open Dashboard → Context to select a Project, Activity, and optional Assignment. The Map shows the selected Project’s Locations. Selecting an Activity adds its Routes; selecting an Assignment focuses the view on that team’s work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap a Location marker to open its actions, then choose Detail. Use the Map toolbar’s Edit Locations action to add or move places. Save to keep changes or Cancel to discard them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Locations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the places shown on your Project map.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap":{"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to organize places and work in LinkMap on iOS and the web.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap","kind":"article","role":"collection","title":"LinkMap","type":"topic","url":"/documentation"},"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Activities":{"abstract":[{"text":"An Activity is one round of work within a Project.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Activities","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Activities","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/activities"},"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Assignments":{"abstract":[{"text":"An Assignment names the person, team, crew, or vehicle responsible for work in an Activity.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Assignments","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Assignments","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/assignments"},"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Locations":{"abstract":[{"text":"Locations are the places your team needs to find or visit, such as entrances, rooms, checkpoints, or delivery points.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Locations","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Locations","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/locations"},"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Project":{"abstract":[{"text":"A Project brings together the places and activities for one area or shared effort.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Project","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Project","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/project"},"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Regions-and-Layers":{"abstract":[{"text":"Regions divide a Project into broad areas. Layers describe levels or surfaces inside a Region, such as floors in a building.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Regions-and-Layers","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Regions and Layers","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/regions-and-layers"},"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Routes-and-Stops":{"abstract":[{"text":"A Route puts places in the order your team should visit them. Each Stop uses a Location from the Project.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://io.github.endsunset.LinkMap/documentation/LinkMap/Routes-and-Stops","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Routes and Sto